course: dictionary
lesson: 6499
title: Necessary and needed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what you must have. «Necessary» means needed: something you must have or must do. «Water, light and air are necessary for plants to grow.» Plants cannot grow without them, so they are needed.
explain: You can test a meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «needed» in place of «necessary»: «A helmet is needed when you cycle.» It still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
explain: «If necessary» means «if it is needed». «Show all the necessary working» in maths means every step that is needed. Look for phrases like «it is necessary to» and «necessary for» to spot the word in use.
fact: Necessary is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «a necessary step».
fact: «Necessary» means needed: something you must have or must do.
fact: «If necessary» means «if it is needed».
fact: A want is something nice to have but not necessary, such as a toy or sweets.
fact: Spell it with one c and two s's: one collar, two sleeves.
exercise: «Water, light and air are necessary for plants to grow.» What does necessary mean here? | Dangerous | *Needed | Very old | Pretty
exercise: «A helmet is necessary when you cycle.» Which word could replace necessary without changing the meaning? | *Needed | Whispered | Pretty | Optional
exercise: «We will call a doctor if necessary.» What does «if necessary» mean? | *If it is needed | If it is a sunny day | If you have finished your tea | If nobody is looking
test: How many s's are in the word necessary? | One | *Two | None | Three
test: Which of these is necessary rather than just a want? | A sweet treat on Friday | A new toy | A shiny sticker | *Water to drink on a hot day
exam: Which phrase means «if it is needed»? | Necessary if you like | Not necessary at all | Necessary to sleep in | *If necessary
